5:Review convergence for Wave 008 is complete. Review round 02 reports **NO BLOCKING ISSUES** and recommends proceeding with **Proposal Restructure**.
11:- `architecture-audit/wave-plan.md`, Wave 008 entry: scopes the wave to `ThreeView.vue`, `Element2DRenderer3D.ts`, `rendering3D.ts`, and new Three.js scene/geometry/label helpers; target outcome is a lifecycle/composition shell over scene adapters/selectors.
12:- `architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md`: confirms Wave 008 remains valid after Wave 007 and that `ThreeView.vue` / `Element2DRenderer3D.ts` are still the next central rendering-boundary cleanup.
15:- `architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md`: records in-place corrections for shell selected-ID flow, concern-split selectors, grouped replacement/disposal, and CSS2D label lifecycle validation.
16:- `architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md`: found blocking issues but recommended Proposal Restructure after correction.
21:**Selected: Proposal Restructure.**
25:- It best satisfies the Wave 008 target by making `ThreeView.vue` a lifecycle/composition shell and moving domain traversal into an application-owned 3D presentation/read-model boundary.
26:- It prevents `Element2DRenderer3D.ts` from reappearing as a domain-aware renderer under a new name by requiring scene adapters to consume DTOs only.
27:- It aligns with the Wave 007 selector/read-model pattern without reopening Wave 007 implementation.
29:- It has the strongest delete posture: `Element2DRenderer3D.ts`, inline `ThreeView.vue` geometry/mesh helpers, debug logs, raw-`World` scene adapters, repeated scene-child clearing, compatibility shims, and obsolete tests/fixtures must be removed rather than wrapped.
35:Proposal Direct is now an acceptable fallback shape after corrections, but it is rejected for implementation because it still frames the work as a smaller extraction. Wave 008 needs the higher-level application read-model boundary chosen by Proposal Restructure so scene adapters cannot continue to receive `World`, perform selected-guide lookup, or own domain-to-view conversion. Direct’s useful details remain incorporated as implementation constraints where they match Proposal Restructure, especially grouped scene-object replacement, CSS2D label cleanup, and static shell-boundary scans.
43:- Refactor `frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue` into a Vue shell that keeps template controls, refs, injected `World`, display-option reads, selected-ID reads, lifecycle hooks, watchers, and calls into a runtime/facade only.
44:- `ThreeView.vue` must pass `{ world, displayOptions, selectedIds }` or equivalent into the runtime / `threePresentation` boundary.
45:- `ThreeView.vue` must not perform selected-element domain lookup, guide/perpendicular-plane derivation, projection-plane matrix interpretation, domain-to-view coordinate conversion, raw Three.js object construction, CSS2D object creation, or scene-child clearing.
52:- `ThreeSceneHost` owns `THREE.Scene`, `PerspectiveCamera`, `WebGLRenderer`, `CSS2DRenderer`, `OrbitControls`, lights, animation loop, resize, and disposal.
59:- CSS2D labels must be owned by the scene host/registry/adapters with explicit cleanup/replacement semantics.
63:- Delete `frontend/src/services/Element2DRenderer3D.ts` and replace its responsibilities with:
64:  - `PlanarElement3DSelector` or equivalent for domain traversal and DTO production;
68:### Element2DRenderer3D role
71:- No compatibility wrapper or re-export for `Element2DRenderer3D` may remain at wave completion.
72:- Any obsolete tests/fixtures that instantiate `Element2DRenderer3D` with raw `World` must be deleted or replaced with selector/adapter tests.
74:### rendering3D config boundaries
76:- Keep `frontend/src/config/rendering3D.ts` as a low-level rendering configuration boundary.
78:- Do not add speculative per-plane compatibility shims or make `rendering3D.ts` a new mixed domain/adapter hub.
83:- `Guide3DSelector` performs selected-guide eligibility/lookup and emits guide perpendicular-plane DTOs plus guide intersection marker DTOs.
93:- `ProjectionPlane3DSelector.ts` for projection-plane surfaces/grids/meshes/reference axes/auxiliary axes/labels.
94:- `PlanarElement3DSelector.ts` for 2D-on-3D point/line/segment/circle DTOs.
95:- `ReconstructedElement3DSelector.ts` for reconstructed 3D point/line/segment/plane DTOs.
96:- `Guide3DSelector.ts` for selected-guide perpendicular planes/intersections.
97:- `Hinge3DSelector.ts` plus dedicated or projection-plane-owned axis/label concern.
100:A single giant selector file that absorbs all current `ThreeView.vue` and `Element2DRenderer3D.ts` traversal is not accepted.
102:### Wave 007 selector reuse without reopening Wave 007
104:- Reuse Wave 007 patterns and small stable selector/read-model policies where helpful.
105:- Do not modify `SvgCanvas.vue`, `CanvasPresentationSelector`, Paper/SVG rendering, 2D interaction, command/tool behavior, or Wave 007 implementation except for tiny shared pure utility/policy consumption if strictly necessary.
111:- `frontend/src/services/Element2DRenderer3D.ts` and all imports/usages.
112:- Large inline geometry/mesh/render helpers from `frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue`, including fallback grid generation, scene setup body, projection-plane rendering, 2D-on-plane rendering, reconstructed 3D rendering, guide perpendicular-plane/intersection rendering, hinge rendering, reference/auxiliary axes, axis-label creation, inline animation/resize/cleanup logic once delegated.
113:- Repeated `scene.children.filter(...).forEach(scene.remove)` clearing patterns from `ThreeView.vue`; use grouped object replacement instead.
114:- Direct raw-domain traversal from `ThreeView.vue` and scene adapters: `world.projectionPlanes`, `getAll3D*`, `getAllPlanes`, `getAllHingeLines`, `getLine2D`, `realize2D(world)`, `realize3D(world)`, guide predicates, and guide-plane math.
115:- Legacy store access if any remains only from deleted legacy geometry/store paths. UI display/selection store reads may remain in `ThreeView.vue` only as shell inputs.
117:- Placeholder `Element2DRenderer3D.resolveVisualStyle()` defaults/TODOs and infinite-line clipping TODOs, replaced by explicit selector/policy decisions.
119:- CSS2D/group disposal leaks: old orphan-label creation/clearing patterns must be deleted in favor of registry-owned label cleanup/replacement.
131:- `ThreeView.vue` contains no low-level Three.js construction, CSS2D object creation, scene-child clearing, projection-plane mesh helpers, guide/hinge geometry derivation, direct domain collection traversal, `realize2D(world)`, or `realize3D(world)`.
132:- Scene setup lives in `ThreeSceneHost` / `ThreeViewRuntime`, not in `ThreeView.vue`.
135:- `frontend/src/services/Element2DRenderer3D.ts` is absent.
145:- CSS2D label cleanup/replacement on group refresh and disposal.
146:- `ThreeView.vue` shell behavior: mount delegates scene setup, refresh runs on world/display/selection changes, resize delegates, and dispose cleans runtime resources.
159:- CSS2D label cleanup/replacement;
